  "limits": [
    "Production renderer exercised in a declared Node browser-API host with real decoded PNGs; no browser journey claimed.",
    "Frozen anatomical landmarks retain uncertainty, especially final DEATH ±8 source pixels and family ratio approximately±3–4%.",
    "Initial high-spawn HUD occlusion is retained in earlier evidence; presented combat view follows a declared valid lower vehicle start and real pursuit.",
    "Idle four-frame matrix is controller coverage; one isolated0.24second hurt normally shows only the first idle pose.",
    "No landing mechanic, canon-exact franchise certification, full campaign completion or full modular Cheyenne corpus claimed.",
    "Reduced-motion Canvas views were not produced. The separate existing unit suite covers 48 samples, 24 with reduced motion; those are not included in the 51 Canvas captures.",
    "The native EN view retains some French status labels, including REINE AILEE and COQUE, while the instructions are translated. This report does not certify complete EN localization.",
    "The six real-death samples prove controller progression, held final pose, clock decay and invisibility after 2.8 seconds. All five pre-expiry sampled renders have alpha1; the intermediate partial-fade interval was not visually sampled.",
    "Strict equality across native resume is not claimed: the same tiny y round-trip and omission of transient vx/vy occur on parent H and candidate. Guarded draw immutability is a separate successful check.",
    "Visual comparison is bounded to the stated pose, pursuit, corpse and edge fixtures; four edge observations are not an exhaustive traversal of the full campaign."
  ],
